LANGUAGE FOCUS   "Capital"
English working capital is a phrase in which neither word means what it usually means. The capital is not long-term funding, as in cost of capital or capital expenditure; it is the short-term money in the trading cycle. And working does not mean functioning; it means circulating, in the old sense of a sum that works by turning over. Arabic رأس المال العامل carries the same metaphor of a capital that works, and French fonds de roulement is the clearest of the three: a fund that rolls. French also distinguishes usefully between fonds de roulement, which is the funding available, and besoin en fonds de roulement, the need the trading cycle creates — a distinction English blurs by using working capital for both the assets and the gap.
